    "slug": "puntland-president-deni-declares-war-on-piracy-in-coastal-town-speech",
    "summary": "President Said Abdullahi Deni announced a full-scale offensive against pirates during a visit to Hafun, Bari region, vowing to eradicate piracy from Puntland's waters.",
    "content": "Puntland President Said Abdullahi Deni declared a full-scale war against piracy on Saturday, delivering a speech in the coastal town of Hafun in the Bari region. Deni stated that his administration would take decisive action to eliminate piracy and secure Puntland's territorial waters.\n\nThe announcement comes amid renewed concerns over maritime security in the Gulf of Aden and Somali waters. Piracy off the Somali coast had significantly declined after 2012 due to international naval patrols and improved onshore governance. However, recent months have seen a resurgence of attacks, including the hijacking of several vessels, prompting fears of a return to the widespread piracy that plagued the region a decade ago.\n\nPresident Deni, who has led Puntland since 2019, has previously emphasized security and development. His speech in Hafun, a historic port town near the Red Sea, underscores the strategic importance of safeguarding Puntland's coastline. The region has long been a hotspot for pirate activity, with groups using its shores as launching points for attacks on commercial shipping.\n\nFor the Somali diaspora, the reemergence of piracy poses significant risks. Many diaspora members rely on remittances and trade routes that pass through these waters, and increased piracy could disrupt livelihoods and raise shipping costs. Additionally, the diaspora often serves as a bridge between Somalia and the international community, and stability in Puntland is crucial for fostering investment and development.\n\nThe international community has yet to respond to Deni's declaration, but naval forces from various countries continue to patrol the area. Local fishermen and traders in Hafun have expressed support for the president's stance, hoping it will bring safety and economic stability. The effectiveness of Deni's pledge will depend on coordinated efforts between Puntland's forces and international partners.\n\nRead the original report from Horseed Media here: https://horseedmedia.net/madaxweyne-deni-oo-ku-dhawaaqay-dagaal-ka-dhan-ah-burcad-badeedda/425576/",
