    "title": "Sagal Cabdi-Wali Selected as Labour Candidate for Holborn and St Pancras",
    "original_title": "Sagal Cabdi-Wali oo loo doortay musharraxa Labour ee kursigii Keir Starmer",
    "slug": "sagal-cabdi-wali-selected-as-labour-candidate-for-holborn-and-st-pancras",
    "summary": "Sagal Cabdi-Wali has been chosen as Labour's parliamentary candidate for Holborn and St Pancras, a seat currently held by Keir Starmer. If elected, she would become the first Somali-born MP in the UK.",
    "content": "On Wednesday evening, 9 September, local Labour Party members in Holborn and St Pancras officially selected Sagal Cabdi-Wali as their parliamentary candidate for the next general election. The constituency is currently represented by Labour leader Keir Starmer, who is expected to step down as MP if he becomes prime minister.\n\nCabdi-Wali, 42, was born in Somalia and came to the UK as a child with her family, who were refugees. She has been active in local politics for several years. In 2022, she was elected as a councillor for Camden Council, and since May she has served as the leader of the council. Before entering politics, she worked on community issues and local policy.\n\nHer selection is notable because Holborn and St Pancras is a safe Labour seat, meaning the chosen candidate is very likely to become an MP at the next general election. If elected, Cabdi-Wali would become the first Somali-born Member of Parliament in the UK, a significant milestone for Somali communities across the country.\n\nFor the Somali diaspora, this represents a major step in political representation. While Somalis have long contributed to British society, they have been underrepresented in national politics. Cabdi-Wali's candidacy offers a high-profile role model for young Somalis and signals growing integration and influence within mainstream political parties.\n\nLabour's selection process involved local party members voting in a meeting on Wednesday evening. The move comes as the party prepares for a general election expected next year, with Starmer widely tipped to become the next prime minister. Cabdi-Wali's background in local government and community work is likely to be central to her campaign.\n\nRead the original report from Goobjoog here: https://goobjoog.com/2026/09/10/sagal-cabdi-wali-oo-loo-doortay-musharraxa-labour-ee-kursigii-keir-starmer/",
